"\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n## Review\nA Sydney Italian restaurant famous for its wood-fired bread.  \nKnown for always having long waits, but we lucked out walking in and were seated immediately.\n\nThe restaurant was quite large with plenty of staff.  \nEverything seemed well organized, and a floor manager was clearly overseeing the whole dining room.\n\nOne unique touch: when your food is ready, you clap to signal a server,  \nand before they bring it to the table, the manager personally comes over to drizzle salt and olive oil.\n\nThe ordering format is built around the wood-fired bread as the base, then you pick the toppings to go with it.  \nWe kept it simple with tomato and burrata cheese.  \nFresh out of the oven, the fluffy bread with cheese, salt, and olive oil was an absolutely perfect combination.\n\nFor pasta, we went with the prawn-based gnocchetti.  \nThe salty seafood and prosciutto worked beautifully together, and the garlic shoots added a great crunch.  \nEverything was cut to similar sizes, making each bite easy to enjoy — and it was the best pasta I've ever had for my taste.\n\nThe locals at the next table were also going hard on cotoletta-style dishes.  \nHighly recommended overall.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"